{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request de0cd410: the caller supplies the key, and Explore\ncomputes the version. No local exploration identity.\n\n1. `actExplore` takes a `key` beside the act and the context. The\n   key is a string that the caller chooses, as section 7.1 of the\n   note says for an authorization. It carries no authority, and\n   Explore retains nothing.\n2. Explore computes the version. Section 7.1 defines a version's\n   `id` as the digest of the act as written, and a retained act is\n   bound. Explore binds the act (section 5.3), so only Explore\n   knows the bound act. The version is the digest of the `act` of\n   the result. A caller cannot state it first.\n3. Define that digest once, in `packages/client`: the SHA-256 of\n   the canonical bytes of `kind`, `on`, `fields` and `expected`,\n   with each symbolic name as written. E4 uses the same function\n   for `Version.id`.\n4. The source of the explored act is `{ key, version }`. `opens`,\n   each `{ output }`, each `{ after }` and each `{ entry }` in the\n   hypothetical view use it. The admitted result also states it, as\n   a new member `source`. I amend sections 3, 5.3 and 8.1 of the\n   note for this.\n5. The key is required. An exploration with no key cannot name the\n   item that an `open` makes, so `opens` has no value.\n6. What each caller supplies:\n   - The MCP tool `explore` (E2) takes the same key argument that\n     the act tool takes, and it is required. An agent that submits\n     with that key gets the names that it explored.\n   - The local instance (E3) supplies the key of the draft or of\n     the request. E3 states how the instance keeps one key from an\n     exploration to its submit.\n   - A test supplies any fixed string.\n7. Equal keys with equal acts and equal contexts give equal\n   explorations. Invariant 9 compares consequences, and a name\n   counts as a consequence, so the test uses the key of the real\n   submit.\n\nThis ruling adds no kernel part. The export of 12dff549 judges an\nintent body under a context and takes no key. The key and the\ndigest live in `packages/client`.\n\nYour lockfile plan stands: C3 carries the client-to-derive edge\nbefore the E1 gate.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:de0cd410f6e2543523bcb4c4213b38056111f6f9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c2d3b4bab05912804bc48129712cd98f805758, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d96cd732ff547fa8959619d6df87c5953f2ded, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d76705dfdd74d8de0047a7a257da83b75d575e2 and 73 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}